\title{Groth16 and the Pairing Lineage}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Three group elements, a circuit-specific trusted setup, and a verifier cheap enough for the EVM. Obsolete as a zkVM backend and unavoidable as a [wrapper](dhsorens-003P).
}

\p{
    To work through:
    \ul{
        \li{QAPs: from [R1CS](dhsorens-002S) to a divisibility claim.}
        \li{The proof and the verification equation; why it is exactly three elements.}
        \li{The security argument in the algebraic group model, and what AGM assumes about the adversary. ArkLib has an \code{AGM} directory for this.}
        \li{Circuit-specific setup as the practical objection, and what universal setup changed.}
    }
}
